          "name": "pqs:context",
          "value": "The repository references P-384 and P-521 curves in pretrained model configuration dictionaries (ViT-B-16-SigLIP-384, ViT-L-16-SigLIP-384, etc.). These are classical elliptic curve cryptography algorithms that are quantum-vulnerable. The configuration points to models that use these curves for key establishment, which would be susceptible to Shor's algorithm once quantum computers become capable of factoring large integers."
